            "Using a greenhouse for your plants in and of itself does not affect global warming significantly. This question might seem to confuse the concept of the greenhouse effect with the use of a physical greenhouse. A greenhouse is a structure with walls and roof made chiefly of transparent material, such as glass, in which plants requiring regulated climatic conditions are grown. While it creates a controlled environment for plants, a single personal or commercial greenhouse does not contribute to global warming on a scale comparable to the global greenhouse effect caused by increased greenhouse gases in the Earth's atmosphere. The impact on global warming from a greenhouse would come from the energy used to heat or cool the structure if it comes from fossil fuel sources."
