            "A rainbow is observed after rain due to the refraction, dispersion, and reflection of sunlight in water droplets. The light is refracted as it enters the water droplet, spreads out into a spectrum of colors, and reflects off the inside surface of the droplet. When it exits the droplet, it is refracted again, and the dispersion of light makes the colors of the rainbow visible.",
            "The phases of the Moon are caused by the relative positions of the Earth, Moon, and Sun. As the Moon orbits Earth, we see different portions of the side of the Moon that is illuminated by the Sun. This results in the various phases from new Moon, to first quarter, full Moon, and last quarter.",
