            "Seasons are experienced due to the tilt of Earth's axis in relation to its orbit around the Sun. This tilt causes different parts of Earth to receive varying amounts of sunlight throughout the year. When the Northern Hemisphere is tilted towards the Sun, it experiences summer, while the Southern Hemisphere experiences winter, and vice versa."
