            "Not all marine mammals live exclusively in water. While some, like the blue whale and dolphins, spend all their time in the ocean, others, such as seals and sea lions, spend a significant amount of time on land. They often come ashore to rest, breed, or give birth, returning to the water to feed.",
            "Marine mammals have a range of adaptations that allow them to thrive both on land and in water. For example, seals and sea lions have streamlined bodies and powerful flippers that make them agile swimmers, yet they can also maneuver on land using their flippers to propel themselves. Additionally, they have a layer of blubber for insulation against cold ocean temperatures and a specialized circulatory system to conserve oxygen during deep dives."
