                "One day a dragon and a dinosaur met in the late Jurassic period. The dragon said, \"I'm stronger than you!\" The dino said, \"I'm the strongest dino ever!\" The next day, the dinosaur and the dragon met in the forest. The dragon made half of a tree fall down with its big claws and fiery breath. The dragon said, \"You can't beat that!\" The dinosaur started running toward a huge tree. The dinosaur rammed the huge tree with its head. Nothing happened. The dragon laughed. Then the tree started to fall. The dragon just stared in total surprise. What moral can you infer from this story?"
