        "image_3": "",
        "image_4": "",
        "extra": {
            "user_audio_transcripts": [
                "A tortoise desired to change its place of residence, so he asked an eagle to carry him to his new home, promising her a rich reward for her trouble. The eagle agreed and seizing the tortoise by the shell with her talons soared aloft. On their way, they met a crow, who said to the eagle: \"Tortoise is good eating.\" \"The shell is too hard,\" Said the eagle in reply. \"The rocks will soon crack the shell,\" Was the crow's answer; and the eagle, taking the hint, let fall the tortoise on a sharp rock, and the two birds made a hearty meal of the tortoise. What moral can you infer from this story?"
            ],
            "raw_question": "",
            "raw_options": [],
            "role_name": "",
            "user_audio_emotion": ""
        }
