        "ref_answers": [
            "[\"Look, this ain't a piece of cake, but let's break it down - apple and orange. Yeah, they're both fruits, like me and you, but it's more than that. They both got that roundness, appeal to the eye, and most importantly you can grab them on the go. No knife, no messy peeling bullshit like some bananas. It's the simplicity and convenience, that's where the damn similarity lies; apple and orange are your words.\", \"This isn't about fruits, this is about the law of simplicity and similarities! You may have different kinds of fruits--an apple, a banana, an orange. Now, let's talk context, keeping it as simple as possible. We're seeing these fruits are all everyday items in a sense. They have mass appeal, easy to find and are healthy. We ain't just talking about mixing random fruits into a boring fruit salad! Apples and oranges, they're the two most similar. Why? They're both round, both can be eaten raw, both have that juicy crunch that leaves you refreshed. Bananas, though, they're a different story, they're kind of the odd one out if you catch my drift. So, if we gotta pinpoint two out of these three, it's the apple and orange that are most similar. Easy, right?\", \"Alright, first off, you've gotta understand what you're dealing with here. You've got three fruits, right? Apple, banana, orange. Now, on a surface level, they might look different, but strip away the peel, and you got similar juicy cores, right? But within the context of the article, apples and oranges, they’re more similar. Both can be squeezed into juice, both are often used as staple examples of fruits and both share a similar shape. The banana, it’s a bit of an outsider here, more distinct in shape and not common juice material. Takes a little more finesse to handle a banana, if you catch my drift. So, in this context, I'd say the apple and the orange are the most similar.\\n\", \"Alright, alright, alright, my friend. You're talking about fruits, right? So, you've got an apple, a banana, and an orange. Now look, in the grand scheme of things, all good, all tasty, right? But when you put 'em side by side, you gotta see the apples and oranges in the same light. Why? They both got that same round shape, that same crisp bite when you sink your teeth into 'em. A banana? It's a whole different ball game, different shape, different texture. So, in the context of our little fruit salad, the apple and the orange, they're the most similar.\", \"Apple and orange, no question. When we're talking fruits, those are the go-to picks, the real moneymakers of the produce world, if you will. Bananas? They're just the filler you need when the main players aren't enough. But apples and oranges? They're the blue-chips of the fruit market, always reliable, always in demand. So, let's just say, if fruits were stocks, I'd be selling apple and orange hard.\"]"
        ],
