        "ref_answers": [
            "['Listen up, pal, it\\'s not rocket science. The SDGs came after the MDGs, you got that part right. But to say the SDGs are an \"extension\" of the MDGs, well, that\\'s a stretch. Are they related? Sure. But the text doesn\\'t tell us whether the SDGs are an extension of the MDGs. It\\'s just not there. So, I\\'d say not enough information is provided to confirm that statement. Got it?', \"Yeah, sure, seems like the SDGs are an extension of the MDGs. The MDGs were the old school, the starting point, right? Then, along comes 2015, and the UN says 'let's ramp it up a bit', and boom, we've got ourselves the SDGs. So, yeah, I'd say that statement in paragraph B is true.\", 'Well, that\\'s not entirely right, is it? The SDGs might have followed the MDGs, but saying they\\'re just an \"extension\" simplifies the whole damn thing. The SDGs have a broader scope, more goals, and are not just about poverty alleviation. So, I\\'d say that statement in paragraph B is not completely accurate. It\\'s got a thread of truth but it\\'s not the whole picture. So, the statement is false, my friend.', \"Alright, listen up, because I'm only gonna say this once. The SDGs being an extension of the MDGs, huh? Well, from the info you've given me, it's hard to say for sure. Yeah, the MDGs were there first, and then came the SDGs. But does that make 'em an extension? Not necessarily, right? Could be a whole new game plan. Without more details, I can't confirm or deny that. So, my verdict? Not enough information.\", \"Well, look here, it seems like you've got your facts a little tangled up. While it's true that the SDGs came after the MDGs, it ain't exactly right to call them an 'extension'. Sure, they share a common aim - making the world a better place, but the SDGs are broader, more ambitious. They're not just an 'extension', they're a whole new game plan. So, to answer your question, there ain't enough information in that there paragraph to say that SDGs are an extension of the MDGs.\"]"
        ],
