            "user_audio_transcripts": [
                "You will hear two short paragraphs, called Paragraph A and Paragraph B. Listen carefully. After hearing both paragraphs, decide if the information in Paragraph A shows that the statement in Paragraph B is true, false, or if there is not enough information to decide. Paragraph A says:  In 2015, the United Nations adopted 17 Sustainable Development Goals, also known as SDGs. Before these, there were targets called the Millennium Development Goals, or MDGs, which were set for the year 2015. The Millennium Development Goals were created at a United Nations summit in the year 2000, and they included eight goals focused on reducing poverty. Paragraph B says:  The SDGs are an extension of the MDGs."
            ],
            "raw_question": "In this task, you are given two short paragraphs A and B. The task is to determine if paragraph A proves that the statement in paragraph B is true, false or not enough information is provided.\nParagraph A: \nIn 2015, the United Nations adopted 17 Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs). \nThese goals had predecessor targets known as the Millennium Development Goals (MDGs), which were established for the year 2015. \nThe Millennium Development Goals were created at a UN summit in 2000 with eight goals focused on poverty alleviation.\n\nParagraph B: The SDGs are an extension of the MDGs.",
