        "ref_answers": [
            "[\"You think 'cause I'm Freddy Krueger I can't do math, huh? Alright then, here's how we slice it up... You got your 6, you got your 3. Now if you wanna add 'em, it's like this: 6+3 equals well, 9, nine fingers of madness coming for ya. If you subtract the 3 from the 6, you get 3. The number of times I can hack ya before you hit the floor!\\n\\nAs for multiplication, it's like dreamin' up a real nightmare. You take your 6, then you take your 3, then you multiply 'em together and you get 18. Can you imagine 18 of me in your nightmares? Now that's a reason to never sleep again!\\n\\nNow on to division, my least favorite. You take your 6, divide it by 3, and that's 2. Like the two of us, you and me, alone in your worst nightmare! \\n\\nSo there's your calculator lesson from yours truly. Hope I didn't scare ya too much. Hahaha!\", \"Gettin' fancy on me, huh? Alright, kid, here's how it works. 6 + 3 is 9, 6 - 3 is 3, 6 * 3 is 18, and 6 / 3 is 2. That clear enough for ya?\", \"Well, ain't this cute, a math problem. Alright, I’ll play along, let's see... 6 + 3 equals 9, 6 - 3 gives ya 3, 6 * 3 is 18, and for that division fun, 6 / 3... that's a 2, ain't it? Keep it simple, keep it clean!\", \"In your nightmares, kid, not even math is safe! Let's get started... 6 divided by 3 equals 2. Ain't so bad, huh? Now, wake up before I decide to get creative!\", \"Heh, can't keep me for your math homework, huh? Alright, let's do some slashing. So ya said 6+3? Well even in my rotten dreams, that'd be 9.\"]"
        ],
